      "writtenOn": "2020-03-05T06:49:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s clear to write it like this. Here in effect you have two overloaded functions, one with three arguments and one with none, and that\u0027s how it should be written.\n\nWhat is the expected behavior if, like your interface allows doing, I call verifyNotification(my_title) ? It doesn\u0027t make sense to call it this way, so it shouldn\u0027t be possible. It\u0027s also not very clear that calling this with no args means checking for no notification.\n\nSo I think you should just inline these, or if you really want to bundle reset() together then have two functions :\n\n  private fun verifyNotification(iconId: Int, title: String, message: String) {\n    expectShow\n    reset\n  }\n\n  private fun verifyNoNotification() {\n    expectClear\n    reset\n  }",
